# Normalize line endings on commit, and never convert them on checkout.
#
# The Windows runner checks out with `core.autocrlf=true` by default, so a file
# committed with LF arrives as CRLF. `test/contracts.test.mjs` regenerates
# `contracts/generated/protocol-names.json` and byte-compares it against the
# checked-in copy — the generator writes LF, the working copy held CRLF, and the
# gate failed on Windows only. Reproduced locally by converting the file.
#
# `eol=lf` is the load-bearing half: `text=auto` alone still converts on
# checkout where the platform default says to.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched by the text machinery.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.wasm binary
*.pem binary
